From a18d424e9daa9744eef7e2e3a383b904e9bc71c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leo <leoschlosser@tutamail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:13:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 92/92] power: supply: max17042: clamp the reported capacity to
 100 %

Without a custom fuel gauge model (the Galaxy Note II's MAX17047 has no
cell data in DT) VFSOC reads slightly above 100 % on a full battery, and
userspace (Android's health HAL) shows "101 %".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
index 505a68c26..b2dc015e5 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
@@ -354,7 +354,8 @@ static int max17042_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
 
-		val->intval = data >> 8;
+		/* uncalibrated gauges (no custom model) read slightly above 100 % */
+		val->intval = min(data >> 8, 100U);
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN:
 		ret = regmap_read(map, MAX17042_DesignCap, &data);
-- 
